+
+    /// KNOWN PROCESS-ABORTING BUG (reproducer kept `#[ignore]`d because a stack
+    /// overflow aborts the whole test process — run with `--ignored` to reproduce):
+    ///
+    /// Parsing a deeply nested XML plist succeeds (the parser and `Value` builder are
+    /// iterative), but *dropping* the resulting `Value` overflows the stack: the
+    /// derived drop glue for `Value`/`Vec<Value>`/`Dictionary` recurses once per
+    /// nesting level. A ~700KB XML input of 100,000 nested `<array>`s parses fine and
+    /// then aborts the process when the value goes out of scope. `Clone` and
